  "query_preview": "..The two main weather impacts today will be the Heat \nand the Thunderstorm chances. High temperatures will top out 4-7 \ndegrees above normal today and an Extreme Heat Warning is in effect \nfrom 10 am MST this morning through 8 pm MST Wednesday. For more \ninformation on this product, please refer to PHXNPWTWC. \n\nBlended total precipitable water satellite imagery shows PW values \nranging between 0.90-1.10 inches across the forecast area. That's \nmore than sufficient moisture in place with daytime heating. The \nmodels point to most convective activity east of a Hannagan Meadow \nto Oracle to Nogales line. The Sky Island Mountains and White \nMountains will be the first to fire between noon and 1 pm, with \nactivity in the lower elevations based on outflows. Steering flow \nwill be light today, less than 10 knots, and out of the northeast to \neast. The main threats today will be gusty outflow winds to 40-45 \nmph, blowing dust along Interstate 10 in Cochise County and \nlocalized heavy rainfall with the strongest storms.\n\nThe current forecast is on track. No planned updates to the \ngrids/text products. For more information on the latter periods of \nthe forecast, please refer to PREV DISCUSSION section below.",
